---
description: Global coding standards
alwaysApply: true
---

## YAGNI

Don't build it until you need it.

## DRY

Extract patterns after the second duplication, not before.

## Fail Fast

Explicit errors beat silent failures.

## Simple First

Write the obvious solution; optimize only if needed.

## Delete Aggressively

Less code means fewer bugs.

## Semantic Naming

Always name variables, parameters, and API endpoints with verbose, self-documenting names that optimize comprehension for both humans and LLMs, not brevity (e.g. `wait_until_obs_is_saved=true` rather than `wait=true`).
